        ### Variants (data sheet chapter 1)

        One data sheet covers the Hi3521A and the Hi3520D V300: one address map, one set of register blocks. The chips differ as follows.

        | | Hi3521A | Hi3520D V300 |
        |---|---|---|
        | CPU | Cortex-A7, up to 1.1 GHz, NEON and FPU | Cortex-A7, up to 800 MHz, NEON and FPU |
        | Caches | 32 KB L1 I + 32 KB L1 D, 128 KB L2 | same |
        | DDR | one 32-bit DDR3/DDR3L controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 512 MB | one 16-bit DDR3/DDR3L controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 512 MB (brief data sheet) |
        | SATA | 2 x SATA 3.0 | 2 x SATA 2.0 |
        | H.264 | enc 4x1080p@30 + 4xCIF@30 + dec 1x1080p@30; dec 5x1080p@30 or 10x720p@30 | enc 4x720p@30 + 4xCIF@30 + dec 4x720p@30; dec 2x1080p@30 or 4x720p@30 |
        | Video input (VI) | four 8-bit or two 16-bit ports (up to 16xD1/960H, 16x720p, 8x1080p TDM) | two 8-bit or one 16-bit port (up to 8xD1/960H, 8x720p, 4x1080p TDM) |
        | Package | TFBGA, 19 x 19 mm, 0.8 mm pitch | Epad-LQFP256, 28 x 28 mm, 0.4 mm pitch |
        | Supplies | core 1.1 V, CPU 1.25 V, I/O 3.3 V, DDR 1.5 V; 3 W typical | core and CPU 1.15 V, I/O 3.3 V, DDR 1.5 V; 2.5 W typical |
        | Common | H.264 baseline/main/high decode L4.2 and encode L5.1, MJPEG/JPEG, IVE, HDMI 1.4 + VGA + CVBS (1080p@60), one HD and one SD graphics layer plus a 128x128 cursor, 3 unidirectional I2S/PCM, integrated audio codec, 1 gigabit Ethernet (RGMII/RMII/MII, TSO), 2 USB 2.0 host, 3 UART, 1 SPI (2 CS), IR, I2C, GPIO, SPI NOR/NAND (1/2/4 bit, 2 CS), 4 KB BOOTROM + 16 KB SRAM, AES/DES/3DES, RTC | |

        ### Boot (data sheet 1.3)

        * BOOTROM_SEL (pin MDCK) = 1: boot from the BOOTROM, which starts the serial download mechanism (HiTool); if the serial link times out the chip boots from the external SPI NAND/NOR flash.
        * BOOTROM_SEL = 0: boot from the external SPI NOR/NAND flash (SFC).

        ### Chip ID

        | Chip | System controller ID registers (0xEE0 .. 0xEEC) | Value read as SC_SYSID |
        |---|---|---|
        | hi3520dv300 | SYSID0..3 reset values from the RDL | 0x3521A100 |
        | hi3521av100 | SYSID0..3 reset values from the RDL | 0x3521A100 |

        The four 8-bit registers form the 32-bit chip ID (SYSID3 is the most significant byte). The values are the reset values of the register descriptions: one data sheet documents one ID for all chips it covers, so the chips of a shared data sheet are not distinguished here (the real value of each variant is not stated).

        ### Memory map notes (data sheet 1.3, Table 1-2)

        * 0x00000000-0x03FFFFFF (64 MB) is the boot window: it points to the boot address space (BOOTROM or the SFC NAND/NOR memory space) while the remap is active and to the on-chip RAM after SC_CTRL remapclear (the Hi3520D V100 data sheet words the same mechanism).
        * BOOTROM window 0x04000000 (4 KB implemented), on-chip RAM window 0x04010000 (16 KB implemented).
        * SFC NAND/NOR memory window 0x14000000-0x14FFFFFF (16 MB); FMC registers at 0x10000000.
        * DDR: 0x80000000-0xFFFFFFFF address space (2 GB); the Hi3521A 32-bit bus supports up to 1 GB, the Hi3520D V300 16-bit bus up to 512 MB (1.2.14).
        * Blocks without register chapter in the data sheet but with a memory-map entry: SCD 0x10080000, DDRT0 0x12100000, HDMI 0x13010000, AVC0/AVC1 H.264 codecs 0x13040000 / 0x13100000, TDE, IVE, JPGD, VGS, VPSS, JPGE (see the register-block table: these are not modelled).

        ### DMA request lines (data sheet 3.6, Table 3-10)

        One DMAC (PL080-style, register block DMAC at 0x10060000, interrupt 42): 4 channels, 2 AHB masters, 16 hardware request lines; each peripheral has a burst (DMACBREQ) and a single (DMACSREQ) request, selected per channel in DMAC_Cn_CONFIG src_periph / dest_periph. Memory has no request line (always ready).

        | Line | Peripheral | Line | Peripheral |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 0 | UART0 RX | 8 | I2C RX |
        | 1 | UART0 TX | 9 | I2C TX |
        | 2 | UART1 RX | 10-15 | Reserved |
        | 3 | UART1 TX | | |
        | 4 | UART2 RX | | |
        | 5 | UART2 TX | | |
        | 6 | SSP RX | | |
        | 7 | SSP TX | | |

        Idle cycles are inserted after each bus operation on channels 2 and 3, so memory-to-memory transfers should use those two channels (data sheet recommendation).

        ### Pin multiplexing summary (PINMUX at 0x120F0000)

        Generated from the pin mux registers of this description (register offsets are relative to the block base; the function lists are the value-ordered choices of each register). Pads that repeat a pattern in consecutive registers are merged into one row.

        | Pads | Mux register (offset from 0x120F0000) | Function choices (value 0, 1, ...) |
