        Pad drive-strength and pull controls are in the separate pad control registers of the same description (not repeated here).

        ### Power, reset and clock modes (data sheet 3.1, 3.2)

        * Resets: hard reset npor from the RSTN pin or the internal POR modules (POR_CORE / POR_IP, selected by POR_SEL; the low pulse must last more than 130 ms, XIN stable); global soft reset sys_rst_n (system controller, level-1 reset control; at least 130 system clock cycles); per-module soft resets xx_rst_n (CRG PERI_CRG registers, level-2 reset control), not released automatically. Diagram: reset tree.
        * A7/DDR/bus clocks start from the 24 MHz crystal; a PLL may be reprogrammed only while the system runs from the crystal; stable 0.1 ms after the change; the lock bits are in PERI_CRG34[4:0] (data sheet 3.2.5, as printed; INFERRED to be the PLL status register of this chip).
        * Spread spectrum control per PLL: VPLL0 PERI_CRG37, VPLL2 PERI_CRG38, APLL PERI_CRG39, EPLL PERI_CRG40, DPLL PERI_CRG46 (bits 11:0 ssmod_cfg).
        * Several modules use a skip-cycle clock divider (clkskipcfg 5 bits + clkloaden load strobe): VEDU0 PERI_CRG15, VEDU1 PERI_CRG16, VPSS PERI_CRG17, TDE PERI_CRG18, VGS PERI_CRG19, JPGE/VOIE PERI_CRG20, JPGD PERI_CRG21, MDU PERI_CRG22.
        * The data sheet has no separate power-domain table or low-power chapter text in the range read for this note; PMC (0x120E0000) is the power-management register block (modelled).

        ### Clock-gate and reset map (generated from the CRG registers)

        | Offset | Register | Description | Gate / reset fields |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 0x028 | PERI_CRG10 | PERI_CRG10 | pclkdbg_cken, arm_core_srst_req, arm_dbg_srst_req, etm_srst_req, l2_srst_req, socdbg_srst_req, cs_srst_req |
        | 0x02C | PERI_CRG11 | PERI_CRG11 | vi0_cken, vi0_srst_req, vi1_cken, vi1_srst_req, vi2_cken, vi2_srst_req, vi3_cken, vi3_srst_req, vi_ppc_srst_req, vi_bus_srst_req, ... |
